 "final_text_tail": "ch puts observed groups first and unobserved groups last. If the ids and the reordered index don't line up, `get_group` returns another group's rows. `BaseGrouper.indices` builds its lookup from `ping.codes` and `self.levels`, so it is the next place to check. `get_indexer_dict` in `pandas/core/sorting.py` is a less likely candidate.\n\n{\"files\": [\"pandas/core/groupby/ops.py\", \"pandas/core/sorting.py\", \"pandas/core/groupby/groupby.py\"], \"functions\": [\"BaseGrouper.result_index_and_ids\", \"BaseGrouper.indices\", \"BaseGrouper._unob_index_and_ids\", \"get_indexer_dict\", \"BaseGrouper._ob_index_and_ids\"]}",
